    {
      "id": "overview-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Boliviq iOS Screens \u2014 Canons BB01\u2013BB19\n\nNumbering follows the canon-index convention: BB{canon #}-{screen seq}, e.g. BB05-02 = Canon BB05 (CRM & Pipeline), 2nd screen in that flow. Canon numbers match claude/canon-index.md.\n\nFrame: iPhone viewport (390x844pt). No fake iOS status bar or keyboard is drawn \u2014 that space is left for the real system chrome, per Apple HIG. Tab bars and nav bars ARE app content and are drawn. Static mockups (not yet wired for interaction), \"core flow\" scope \u2014 5\u20137 screens per canon covering that canon's key journeys, not every possible screen."
    },
