    {
      "id": "ios-compliance-note",
      "x": 3400,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "iOS App Store compliance flagged in these mockups:\n\n\u2022 BB02-02 Sign Up \u2014 Sign in with Apple shown alongside Google (Guideline 4.8: any third-party login requires an equivalent Apple option).\n\n\u2022 BB02-06 Subscription \u2014 digital plan upgrades on iOS must use Apple In-App Purchase / StoreKit (Guideline 3.1.1); Stripe stays web-only. Matches canon-mobile-pwa.md's payment rule.\n\n\u2022 BB01-04 Settings \u2014 in-app \"Delete account\" row is the required self-service deletion path (Guideline 5.1.1(v)).\n\n\u2022 BB11-01 Location Priming and BB11-02 Document Scanner (Canon BB11) show the permission-priming and camera-capture patterns Apple expects ahead of the system prompt \u2014 no fake status bar or keyboard drawn on either, per Apple HIG.\n\nNot yet mocked but needed before submission: push-notification opt-in priming and biometric (Face ID) fallback-to-password state."
    },
    {
      "id": "compliance-note-2",
      "x": 3400,
      "y": 3072,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "Communication compliance (Canon BB04):\n\n\u2022 BB04-04 bakes in the canon's rule directly \u2014 quiet hours, SMS consent, and an opt-out (STOP) control live in Settings, not buried per-feature.\n\n\u2022 BB04-05 Report/Block implements the canon's spam-reporting and blocking requirement."
    },
    {
      "id": "compliance-note-3",
      "x": 3400,
      "y": 5120,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "Trust & Verification compliance (Canon BB06):\n\n\u2022 BB06-01 and BB06-02 both carry an explicit disclaimer that a verification badge confirms a document was submitted, not that Boliviq guarantees the professional's work \u2014 this is a hard rule in canon-trust-verification.md, not optional copy.\n\n\u2022 BB06-05 repeats the same disclaimer at the complaint level: a dispute outcome never changes a verification badge."
    },
    {
      "id": "compliance-note-4",
      "x": 3400,
      "y": 6144,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "AI Features compliance (Canon BB07):\n\n\u2022 BB07-02 and BB07-03 both surface the canon's autonomy limits (agents never send messages, sign agreements, move money, or publish listings without confirmation).\n\n\u2022 BB07-04 is that confirmation gate made concrete \u2014 every outbound AI action stops here first.\n\n\u2022 BB07-05 shows the credit ledger mechanics required by the canon: reserve \u2192 charge/release, with an idempotency key."
    },
    {
      "id": "compliance-note-9",
      "x": 3400,
      "y": 8192,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "Integrations compliance (Canon BB09):\n\n\u2022 BB09-02 MLS/IDX detail carries the canon's hard rule verbatim \u2014 off-market listings are never labeled or displayed as MLS listings unless received through an authorized MLS integration."
    },
    {
      "id": "compliance-note-14",
      "x": 3400,
      "y": 13312,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "Realtor compliance (Canon BB14):\n\n\u2022 BB14-03 CMA Workspace labels its suggested price range as a pricing estimate from comparable sales, not a licensed appraisal \u2014 consistent with the same rule applied to investor tools in Canon BB15."
    },
    {
      "id": "compliance-note-15",
      "x": 3400,
      "y": 14336,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "Investor & Wholesaler compliance (Canon BB15):\n\n\u2022 BB15-01 Deal Calculator discloses that automated valuations and offer calculations are estimates, not licensed appraisals.\n\n\u2022 BB15-03 Disposition carries a state-sensitive compliance notice \u2014 wholesaling, marketing equitable interests, licensing and disclosure requirements vary by jurisdiction, per canon-profile-investor-wholesaler.md."
    },
    {
      "id": "compliance-note-16",
      "x": 3400,
      "y": 15360,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "Lender compliance (Canon BB16):\n\n\u2022 BB16-02 Prequalification is explicit that this is a prequalification estimate only \u2014 not a lending decision or commitment to lend. Boliviq does not make lending decisions unless separately licensed to do so."
    },
    {
      "id": "compliance-note-18",
      "x": 3400,
      "y": 17408,
      "w": 340,
      "text": "Transaction Professionals compliance (Canon BB18):\n\n\u2022 BB18-01 Inspection Report states AI can generate repair requests from findings but never edits or alters the inspector's signed report.\n\n\u2022 BB18-02 Appraisal Status separates the licensed appraisal from Boliviq's own automated value estimate \u2014 only the licensed report is used for lending decisions.\n\n\u2022 BB18-03 Secure Closing Room carries an explicit anti-wire-fraud warning \u2014 Boliviq and the title company will never change wiring instructions by email or text.\n\n\u2022 BB18-05 Attorney Consultation states plainly that Boliviq AI is not an attorney and does not provide legal advice \u2014 it only routes requests to a licensed professional."
    }
